{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Altretamine is linked to Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn is associated with Tretamine and Belotecan, both of which are indicated to cause Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma. This implies a potential role for Altretamine in the development of this cancer, possibly through mechanisms that involve the tumor's biological response to these compounds. The overlapping indications and the shared target of Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma across different pathways suggest a possible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Altretamine may contribute to the progression of Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma via a pathway involving germ cell tumors and their interaction with other chemotherapeutic agents.",
